[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue with one fix queued. Its reports say otherwise.
Read by tenant, by channel and by what each report describes, the ticket holds three problems.
Each needs its own fix, so each has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October: the parser fix shipped, and booking-v3 was retired, so its
hint will not be fixed. Neither touches the one-day moves. That ticket is still open.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} {status} />

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser read dates month first.** Every tenant on file writes the day
first, so a booking for 7 April went out for 4 July. This is the bug #4471 was opened for.
Fixed by `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.

**`hint`: booking-v3 told people to type the month first.** Under its date field, booking-v3
printed `MM/DD/YYYY`; booking-v2 prints `DD/MM/YYYY`. On a day-first tenant, people typed what the
hint said and the form read it the tenant's way, so the date flipped just like a parser report.
It only happened through the `form` channel of booking-v3 tenants, and the parser fix does not
touch it. Won't fix: booking-v3 is retired, so no new report can come in this way.

**`one-day`: the date moves by one day.** These reports describe a booking that lands a day
off, not a day and month swapped: "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday."
The desk already read them this way (`desk-notes.json`), but `CauseTable` files them under
`parser` because of their tenant. A parser that reads month first cannot move a date by one day,
so the parser fix does not touch them, and they did not come through booking-v3. It looks like a
time-zone conversion; that needs checking. Still open.

## Why one ticket hid three

- The desk merges on subject line alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
  All three problems come in under the same subjects ("Date is wrong", "Wrong day on the invite"),
  so they all merged into #4471.
- Intake's tag is a guess from the reporter's browser, not from the tenant. The "tagged as"
  column shows how often it disagrees with the problem.
- The ticket export comes in pages that overlap, so some reports appear twice. Count by id, once.

## For the desk

- Closing #4471 settled two of the three problems. A new report of a date that moves by one day
  belongs with the open ticket, not with #4471.
- A report about a wrong date is not a duplicate just because its subject matches. Check the
  tenant, the channel and what moved (a day and month swapped, or one day) before you merge.
- Decision 0001 still says to merge on subject alone. A new decision record should replace it.

